Change freezes: under **Workflows → Change Freezes**, set one-time or recurring windows (RRULE, length and time zone, with weekend, nightly, month-end and holiday presets) for all workflows or by category, tag or workflow, with exclusions. During a freeze nothing in a covered workflow runs: launching and scheduling are refused, and a run that comes due is marked the new **Blocked by freeze** status. Banners and lock badges show freezes to anyone who can see the workflow, with a per-freeze "starts soon" warning (2 hours by default). **Override change freezes** lets someone run anyway with a reason stamped on the run, and is also needed for a tag or category change that would take a workflow out of a freeze; Git sync skips such a change with `E-NWE-302`. Includes a REST API with status and preview endpoints, and three new ready-made permissions.
